WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.219
Okay, let's talk about the K-shaped

00:00:02.219 --> 00:00:04.062
economy. The President has proposed

00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:05.663
raising wages, cutting taxes, and

00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:07.358
reducing the burden on the people—

00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:09.154
this policy direction is very clear.

00:00:09.154 --> 00:00:10.998
However, some believe we should find a

00:00:10.998 --> 00:00:12.747
better balance between the first and

00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:14.571
second distribution of wealth. What

00:00:14.571 --> 00:00:16.279
does that mean? Currently, the

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:18.130
government provides many benefits, such

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.656
as subsidies, social welfare, or

00:00:19.656 --> 00:00:21.414
policies for wage increases for local

00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:23.080
workers through extra migrant labor

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.010
quotas. Essentially, it seems companies

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.752
earn the money first, the government

00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:28.636
collects taxes, and then the government

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:30.433
uses those taxes for subsidies. This

00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:32.092
all seems to be part of the second

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:33.894
distribution, while some people place

00:00:33.894 --> 00:00:35.411
greater importance on the first

00:00:35.411 --> 00:00:36.847
distribution. Take the recent

00:00:36.847 --> 00:00:38.510
controversies at companies like Kuai

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.173
Kuai or Micron; they illustrate that

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.926
many workers feel that if a company is

00:00:41.926 --> 00:00:43.409
making huge profits, has already

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.937
received tax breaks, and has even

00:00:44.937 --> 00:00:46.645
received AI subsidies, shouldn't they

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:48.443
distribute a certain percentage of that

00:00:48.443 --> 00:00:50.151
as compensation to the workers within

00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:51.936
the same year? Do you feel that the

00:00:51.936 --> 00:00:53.846
first distribution is a direction the

00:00:53.846 --> 00:00:55.857
government needs to focus on more now?

00:00:55.857 --> 00:00:57.532
For instance, regarding support for

00:00:57.532 --> 00:00:59.253
labor unions, or when many companies

00:00:59.253 --> 00:01:01.021
are receiving subsidies, shouldn't we

00:01:01.021 --> 00:01:02.882
correspondingly demand that "you should

00:01:02.882 --> 00:01:04.939
pay your employees more"? What are your

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:05.550
thoughts?

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.970
>> Alright, thank you. I believe that

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.246
management and labor are like fish and

00:01:10.246 --> 00:01:12.634
water; they need each other. Regarding

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.250
the current demands from the labor side

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.867
at Micron, I hope that more time can be

00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:20.411
taken. And that all parties can come to

00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:22.936
the table with greater sincerity. Then,

00:01:22.936 --> 00:01:25.716
work out a solution that both sides can

00:01:25.716 --> 00:01:28.426
accept to foster a win-win outcome for

00:01:28.426 --> 00:01:30.746
labor and management. This would be

00:01:30.746 --> 00:01:32.646
good for the company, good for the

00:01:32.646 --> 00:01:34.818
workers, and actually good for Taiwan's

00:01:34.818 --> 00:01:37.170
overall labor environment. Secondly, as

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.564
you mentioned at the beginning, will

00:01:39.564 --> 00:01:41.957
developing the AI industry lead to a

00:01:41.957 --> 00:01:45.085
K-shaped economy? This is my primary

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:47.475
concern as President, and it is also

00:01:47.475 --> 00:01:49.542
the first point addressed under

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.932
sustainable development in our seven

00:01:51.932 --> 00:01:54.358
core principles of the AI Basic Act.

00:01:54.358 --> 00:01:56.045
That is to say, when developing

00:01:56.045 --> 00:01:57.995
artificial intelligence, we must not

00:01:57.995 --> 00:01:59.414
let the wealth gap widen,

00:01:59.414 --> 00:02:01.695
>> thereby creating a K-shaped economy;

00:02:01.695 --> 00:02:03.820
that is not what we want. We want

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.275
sustainable social development. So, how

00:02:06.275 --> 00:02:08.484
do I plan to do that? The first step is

00:02:08.484 --> 00:02:10.283
to avoid the polarization of Taiwan's

00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:12.259
industries. This means not having only

00:02:12.259 --> 00:02:13.765
the tech industry or only the

00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:15.809
semiconductor and server industries. So

00:02:15.809 --> 00:02:18.537
, we must avoid this polarization—and

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.932
how do I do that? For the first point,

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:22.933
we must pay special attention to the

00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:24.609
fact that beyond assisting the

00:02:24.609 --> 00:02:26.447
continued development of the tech

00:02:26.447 --> 00:02:28.556
industry, we have proposed the Act for

00:02:28.556 --> 00:02:30.502
the Upgrading and Transformation of

00:02:30.502 --> 00:02:32.607
Small and Medium Enterprises. Through

00:02:32.607 --> 00:02:34.732
this legislation, as I mentioned in my

00:02:34.732 --> 00:02:36.858
second-anniversary address on May 20th

00:02:36.858 --> 00:02:38.984
this year, I intend to establish a 100-

00:02:38.984 --> 00:02:39.793
billion fund.

00:02:39.793 --> 00:02:41.086
>> Mm.

00:02:41.086 --> 00:02:43.077
>> To assist small and medium enterprises

00:02:43.077 --> 00:02:45.068
with their upgrading and transformation

00:02:45.068 --> 00:02:47.957
. And the third point is one I consider

00:02:47.957 --> 00:02:50.516
even more important, which is tackling

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:54.516
...
